    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d144">

                <pb facs="0273" n="183" xml:id="pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.51/292</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June 19,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 33</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In a despatch from our Legation at Quito
                    there are transmitted several clippings from Ecuadorean newspapers of May 4,
                        1920,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d144-f1"/> in which it is reported that the
                    “Accorsi Contract” has been approved by the Italian Parliament.</p>
                <p>Referring to Mr. Jay’s despatch No. 1581, of April 14, 1920, in regard to this
                    same matter, the Department requests you to endeavor to obtain and transmit to
                    it a copy and translation of the reported Act of Parliament, together with a
                    copy and translation of the Accorsi project.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A.
                            Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d144-f1" n="7" xml:id="d144-f1-content">
                <p>Only the clippings have been found in Department files.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
